                <h2>Applicable Scenarios and Prerequisites</h2>
<p>This SOP applies when:<br />
- A TikTok Shop listing goes live and needs to go from zero to stable orders within 14 days<br />
- The operations team has ad accounts ready but insufficient creative inventory<br />
- Quick multi-variant testing is required to identify high-converting creatives</p>
<p><strong>Cold Start Pre-Launch Checklist:</strong><br />
- [ ] TikTok Shop storefront fully set up (profile photo, bio, featured product page)<br />
- [ ] Ad account configured with MMM package for multi-asset simultaneous launch<br />
- [ ] Product catalog (SKU, pricing, inventory) synced to the campaign backend<br />
- [ ] Cold start KPIs confirmed: clicks / add-to-carts / first orders target</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 1: Asset Requirement Planning</h2>
<h3>1.1 Define the Asset Matrix</h3>
<p>For cold start, build your asset pool with this recommended ratio:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Asset Type</th>
<th>Share</th>
<th>Primary Purpose</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Product showcase (15-30s)</td>
<td>40%</td>
<td>Highlight core USP, drive volume</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Scenario-based content (30-60s)</td>
<td>30%</td>
<td>Build usage context, increase trust</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Live-action / Unboxing</td>
<td>20%</td>
<td>Boost authenticity, reduce hesitation</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Carousel / Static</td>
<td>10%</td>
<td>Backup combinations, improve CTR</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>1.2 Break Down Production Tasks</h3>
<p>Per SKU, cold start asset pool recommendation:<br />
- Primary SKU: minimum 12-15 video assets<br />
- Secondary SKU: minimum 6-8 video assets</p>
<p><strong>Actions:</strong><br />
1. List each promoted product's core selling points (max 3)<br />
2. Split scripts by USP direction, 3-4 assets per USP<br />
3. Define presentation style for each asset (product close-up / talent / montage)<br />
4. Complete the Asset Requirement Form and sync with design/video team</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 2: Asset Production and Review</h2>
<h3>2.1 Video Production Standards</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Parameter</th>
<th>Requirement</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Duration</td>
<td>9-15s primary (in-feed optimized), 30-60s extended versions</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Aspect Ratio</td>
<td>9:16 vertical (priority), 1:1 horizontal (backup)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Resolution</td>
<td>1080P minimum, avoid heavy compression</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Captions</td>
<td>Mandatory, consistent font, readable size</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Brand Elements</td>
<td>Opening slate max 1s, natural voiceover integration</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>2.2 Asset Naming Convention</h3>
<p>Format: <code>Date_ProductCode_USPTag_Sequence_Version</code></p>
<p>Example: <code>20240115_SKU001_face_01_A.mp4</code></p>
<blockquote>
<p>Consistent naming significantly improves asset reconciliation efficiency and prevents ad plan association errors.</p>
</blockquote>
<h3>2.3 Pre-Upload Review Checklist</h3>
<ul>
<li>[ ] No platform-restricted language (absolute claims, false promises)</li>
<li>[ ] Voiceover matches subtitles</li>
<li>[ ] Product shown matches actual SKU</li>
<li>[ ] Background music royalty-free</li>
<li>[ ] Dimensions meet placement requirements</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 3: Test Grouping and Launch</h2>
<h3>3.1 Campaign Grouping Strategy</h3>
<p>Use a "funnel testing" approach for cold start:</p>
<p><strong>Phase 1 (Days 1-3): Broad Testing</strong><br />
- Create 1 ad group per USP direction<br />
- No duplicate assets across groups<br />
- Set daily budget at 2-3x per group to quickly gather data signals</p>
<p><strong>Phase 2 (Days 4-7): Performance Validation</strong><br />
- Retain assets with CTR &gt; 1.5%, CVR &gt; 3%<br />
- Replicate top performers to check if results scale</p>
<p><strong>Phase 3 (Days 8-14): Stable Scaling</strong><br />
- Concentrate budget on groups showing positive ROAS<br />
- Maintain 20% fresh creative rotation to prevent fatigue</p>
<h3>3.2 Pre-Launch Checklist</h3>
<ul>
<li>[ ] All assets uploaded to Business Manager (BM)</li>
<li>[ ] Asset IDs mapped to naming document</li>
<li>[ ] Ad group naming: <code>Date_Product_TestDirection_AssetID</code></li>
<li>[ ] Pixels installed correctly for conversion tracking</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 4: Data Recovery and Iteration</h2>
<h3>4.1 Key Metrics by Stage</h3>
<p>Monitor daily, segmented by asset:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Stage</th>
<th>Primary Metric</th>
<th>Healthy Benchmark</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Click Phase</td>
<td>CTR</td>
<td>&gt; 1.2%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Conversion Phase</td>
<td>CVR</td>
<td>&gt; 2.5%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Cost Phase</td>
<td>CPA</td>
<td>&lt; 30% of target LTV</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Overall Phase</td>
<td>ROAS</td>
<td>&gt; 1.5 (cold start period)</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>4.2 Asset Performance Scoring</h3>
<p>Export asset data every 3 days, score by:</p>
<pre><code>Composite Score = CTR (40%) + CVR (40%) + Video Completion Rate (20%)
</code></pre>
<ul>
<li>Score &gt; 80: Enter primary asset pool</li>
<li>Score 60-80: Keep for observation, continue testing</li>
<li>Score &lt; 60: Pause, replace with new assets</li>
</ul>
<h3>4.3 Iteration Cadence</h3>
<ul>
<li>During cold start, refresh 30% of asset pool every 5 days</li>
<li>Prioritize replacing assets with CTR below 50% of average</li>
<li>Preserve test data for future product reuse reference</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Quick FAQ</h2>
<p><strong>Q: Enough assets but campaigns still stuck in cold start?</strong><br />
A: Check account historical performance and new account credit score. During cold start, avoid frequent budget changes or pausing — maintain stable delivery for 48+ hours before adjusting.</p>
<p><strong>Q: Multiple new products launching simultaneously, how to allocate assets?</strong><br />
A: Allocate by product priority: Top product gets 60% asset budget, others get 20% each. Avoid "scattered" distribution that leaves nothing running at scale.</p>
<p><strong>Q: Live-action content is expensive, how to balance?</strong><br />
A: During cold start, prioritize product close-ups with captions to validate USP first. Invest in talent production only after direction is confirmed. Suggested ratio: 1 live-action to 3 non-live-action.</p>
